# Testing & Quality Assurance Standards

## 1. Zero-Flakiness Guarantee
- All tests must be 100% deterministic, hermetic, and isolated.
- Never rely on real third-party external networks or live paid API endpoints in automated tests.
- Always mock external HTTP requests, LLM API responses, and external clock timeouts using deterministic mocks (`unittest.mock.patch`, `httpx.MockTransport`, or `pytest-mock`).

## 2. Comprehensive Edge Case Coverage
When adding or updating features, tests must cover:
- **Boundary Conditions**: Empty collections, zero values, negative numbers, maximum string lengths, maximum token limits.
- **Error Pathways**: 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 429 Rate Limit Exceeded, 500 Internal Server Error, 503 Gateway Timeout.
- **Failover & Resilience**: Provider fallbacks, circuit breaker trip and recovery, mid-stream retry behavior.
- **Malformed Input**: Invalid JSON payloads, unexpected data types, missing required fields.

## 3. Preservation of Existing Tests
- **Never weaken or delete tests**: Under no circumstances should an existing test assertion be relaxed, commented out, or removed simply to make a change pass.
- If an existing test fails, treat it as a hard regression signal and fix the underlying implementation.

## 4. Test Execution Commands
- **Python Full Test Suite**:
  ```powershell
  .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py"
  ```
- **Website Production Build & Lint**:
  ```powershell
  cd website
  npm run lint
  npm run build
  ```
